Polished `src/blog/people/drafts/Stable-Ronaldo.md`.

**The main problem was one no script catches: the piece kept stopping to tell the reader how to read it.** Ten instructional directives — "Sit with the word he reached for," "Watch how consistently the equation shows up," "Read the tail of that sentence again," "Notice the phrasing," "Now put the ad load next to the ledger," "Note where this collapse landed," "Go back to the bedroom in 2022," and four more. That's a museum-docent cadence, and it was the loudest AI tell left in the draft. Cut to one (a pointer at a specific timeline row, which is doing real work). Each of the others became a statement that lands the observation itself, or a cut that lets the pull quote / inner-thought do the pivot.

**Second: the negation-then-assertion engine was at 7, not the 3 the `FORMULA FINGERPRINT LEDGER` claimed.** The ledger was stale exactly as the command warns. Rewrote five into positive form, including the empathy turn (which I kept in substance — "Never needing to worry is a different product from happiness" — since the standards protect that beat). Three survive on purpose: the "inventory" pull quote, "The engine is not appetite. It is accounting," and the xQc refusal.

Also cut the comparative seesaws ("would rather absorb a bill than leave one behind" is now causal: *he grew up in the house where somebody left a bill behind and walked out, so he ate this one himself*), split four wall-of-text paragraphs for mobile, and fixed two clauses that fought themselves — notably the Kai Cenat close, where "a bedroom he had not been inside of and had not seen in three years" became "a bedroom he had never stood in, three years after the last time it was on his screen." He watched the room on a stream; he was never in it. That's the whole point of the ending.

**Final counts:** contrast pairs 0 total (0 strong, 0 comparative). blog-lint 0 fail / 1 warn — the warn is the expected "no faqs in frontmatter," since the enrich stage hasn't run. Body 3,704 words. No em-dashes, no banned phrases, `lastmod` and all frontmatter untouched.

**Production-ready on prose.** Two things I left rather than decided for you: heading case is mixed (H2 1–2 sentence case, H2 3–8 Title Case) — the editorial standards want sentence case, but the headings are locked by the `HEADING MIX LEDGER` and match the people-corpus convention, so I flagged it instead of changing it. And the frontmatter enrich stage still needs to run for the FAQs. The three open source questions from the second pass (Ninja's DM still paraphrased, the "I forgive you" line unattributed, the soft Boba date) are unchanged — those need research, not editing.
